# What `gcloud builds submit` must NOT upload as build context.
#
# THIS FILE IS LOAD-BEARING. gcloud only derives exclusions from .gitignore
# when the directory is a git checkout — this one is not, so without an
# explicit .gcloudignore it would upload EVERYTHING: node_modules alone is
# 663 MB, plus emulator data and Terraform state. That is a slow, costly
# upload on every build, and it would push the context past comfortable
# limits for no benefit.
#
# Keep this in step with .dockerignore. They serve different tools —
# .gcloudignore controls what is UPLOADED to Cloud Build, .dockerignore
# controls what the daemon sees as build context once it is there — but
# anything in one almost always belongs in the other.

# --- Dependencies: reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile ----------
# A host node_modules also carries platform-specific binaries (sharp's
# libvips), which would be wrong for a linux/amd64 image anyway.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# --- Build output: recompiled in the image ---------------------------------
dist/
**/dist/
dist-gallery/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Local development state -----------------------------------------------
.emulator-data/
coverage/
.vite/
*.log

# --- Infrastructure state: secrets and machine-specific values -------------
infra/.terraform/
infra/.terraform.lock.hcl
infra/*.tfstate
infra/*.tfstate.*
infra/terraform.tfvars

# --- Local env files --------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
apps/web/.env.development

# --- Not needed to build a Node server image -------------------------------
.firebase/
*.png
*.pdf
